  "verbalization": "Ponasterone A appears to interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Ponasterone A acts as a target for Annexin A1, which in turn is a target of Cyclotryprostatin B or 6-Bromo-8-Methoxy-4-Oxo-1H-Quinoline-2-Carboxylic Acid. Both of these molecules are implicated in targeting Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, indicating a potential role for Ponasterone A in modulating the activity of this enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Ponasterone A influences Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a dependency on the downstream targets, suggesting that Ponasterone A may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions.",
